title: "Practical Biopython Course"
message: "If you use these materials, please cite them using the metadata below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Hentabli
    given-names: Hamza
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9530-2815"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hentablihamza/practical-biopython-course"
url: "https://github.com/hentablihamza/practical-biopython-course"
abstract: >
  A hands-on, 12-notebook course that teaches Biopython from Python basics to sequence
  analysis, NCBI Entrez, BLAST, pairwise and multiple alignment, protein analysis,
  phylogenetics, and protein-ligand structures with Bio.PDB, following the drug target EGFR
  with real public data from NCBI, UniProt, and the PDB. Every notebook runs in Google Colab
  with one click.
keywords:
  - Biopython
  - bioinformatics
  - structural biology
  - drug discovery
  - sequence analysis
  - BLAST
  - education
  - tutorial
date-released: "2026-11-24"
